export type { DsColor, DsColorToken } from './utils/color';
```

---

### 3. CHANGELOG.md (Top ~20 lines)

```
# Changelog

All notable changes to `@dooph-software/design-system` will be documented here.

Format: [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/)  
Versioning: [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html)

---

## [Unreleased]

The next release is a major (v6). An item is under **Breaking** when code
written against 5.3.0 stops compiling, when a documented token or class stops
styling, or when a default, a size, a position, a role or an accessible name
that 5.3.0 set changes without a compile error. Each item says what 5.3.0
had, what v6 has, and how to fix the consumer code. Items marked **silent**
raise no compile error: find them by searching for the old name, or for the
token, component or test query the item names. **Changed** holds the rest:
```

The format follows Keep a Changelog with semantic versioning. The current release is v6 (unreleased), breaking from v5.3.0.

---

### 4. Simple Component Using CVA Recipes

The **Sticker** component itself is an excellent simple example of cva usage:

```tsx
const stickerVariants = cva(
  [
    "inline-flex w-fit items-center gap-sm overflow-clip",
    "px-rg whitespace-nowrap",
  ],
  {
    variants: {
      variant: {
        prominent: "bg-sticker-bg-prominent text-sticker-prominent",
        alternate: "bg-sticker-bg-alternate text-sticker-alternate",
        secondary: "bg-sticker-bg-secondary text-sticker-secondary",
        tertiary: "bg-sticker-bg-tertiary text-sticker-tertiary",
        danger: "bg-sticker-bg-danger text-sticker-danger",
        custom: "",
      },
      size: {
        standard: "rounded-tight py-sticker-y",
        micro: "h-button-micro rounded-mini",
      },
    },
    defaultVariants: {
      variant: "prominent",
      size: "standard",
    },
  },
);
```

This shows the cva pattern: base styles, then variant options, default variants, and discriminated union prop types to enforce constraints.

---

### 5. Text Components List

From `src/components/Text/index.ts`, the exported text component names are:

- **BaseText** (the polymorphic primitive, all others are built on it)
- **BodyText**
