Done. Here's the hand-back:

---

```
Lint:              npm run lint → exit 0, "conventions: 30 checks passed"
Generated docs:    node scripts/generate-docs.mjs → components.md, inventory.md, client-references.md
Skill mirrors:     node scripts/sync-skills.mjs → updated inventory.md in .claude/ and .agent/ (2 changes)
Stories:           Operational (alternate/green sticker), Degraded (prominent/purple),
                   Down (danger/red), CustomLabel ("API Gateway"), Micro (micro size),
                   AllStatuses (all three in a column), Sizes (standard + micro)
Header contract:   none — no invariant a reasonable edit would break; the status-to-variant
                   map is a straightforward lookup with no hidden geometry or constraint
New dependency / allowlist entry: none
```

**Design decisions (all open for your review):**

| Decision | Chosen | Alternative | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| Status dot | 6px (`size-xs`) circle with `bg-current` (inherits sticker text colour) | An icon, or no dot | Open — no Figma spec |
| `operational` → variant | `alternate` (teal #13c29f) | `tertiary` (blue), or a custom colour | Open |
| `degraded` → variant | `prominent` (purple #340fd9) | No amber/yellow token exists in the DS; a new token or `custom` with a new colour would be needed for a true warning hue | **Open — most likely to need revision** |
| `down` → variant | `danger` (red #ea3f3f) | n/a — natural fit | Settled |
| Default labels | "Operational" / "Degraded" / "Down" | Different wording, or require `label` | Open |
| `children` excluded from props | Enforced via `Omit<…, "children">` so the badge controls its own content | Allow arbitrary children | Settled |

**Polling belongs to your app.** Here's the consumer-side snippet the component was designed for:

```tsx
"use client";
import { useEffect, useState } from "react";
import {
  ServiceStatusBadge,
  ServiceStatusBadgeStatus,
} from "@dooph-software/design-system";

